        2.3 AddTech Research (PCChip)       

        AddTech  chipsets  are  usually  labelled  &quot;PCChip&quot;  or &quot;Hedaka&quot;.
        AddTech  designs  their  chips for use on their own motherboards,
        and   they  identify  their  chipsets  by  the  motherboard  part
        numbers.   There  is at least one AddTech chipset that is used on
        two   different  motherboards  with  different  motherboard  part
        numbers.   To  avoid  confusion,  The  Last  Byte  Memory Manager
        refers  to  these  chips  using  &quot;PCCHIP&quot;  followed  by  a unique
        number.  

        Part Number     Shadow Ram      Address Range   Organization
        -----------     ----------      -------------   ------------
        PCCHIP1         256k            C0000-FFFFF     16x16k
        PCCHIP2         192k+32k        C0000-EFFFF     12x16k

        Part Number     Manufacturer&#x27;s Description
        -----------     --------------------------
        PCCHIP1         Used on 286/386SX AT motherboards M205 and M209
        PCCHIP2         Used on 386 AT motherboard M321


