        Oct 09, 1994      SHADOW RAM MEMORY CONTROLLERS                16


                     CHAPTER 3 - UNSUPPORTED CHIPSETS       


        If  your computer has shadow ram capability, then it probably has
        a  shadow ram memory controller.  However, some of these chipsets
        cannot  be  supported by The Last Byte Memory Manager for reasons
        shown below.  

        Some  of  these  chips, however, do have hardware EMS support and
        thus  many  of  their motherboards come with an EMS device driver
        designed  specifically  to take advantage of this capability.  So
        in  many  cases,  you can install this driver first, and then The
        Last  Byte  Memory  Manager can use it to manage the upper memory
        area.  


        3.1 No Shadow Ram Support      

        Some   of   the   older   chipsets  do  not  provide  shadow  ram
        capability.  

        Examples: Western Digital chipsets
                  Texas Instruments TACT82300 series
                  Early Suntac chipsets (ST62BC001-6)
                  United Microelectronics Corp. UM82C231


        3.2 Shadow Ram is not Read/Write     

        Some  chipsets  have  shadow ram, but can only put it into either
        write-only  mode  (for copying rom contents to ram), or read-only
        mode  (to  prevent accidental writes into what&#x27;s supposed to be a
        copy  of  rom).  The hardware EMS in some such chipsets sometimes
        provides  a limited amount (e.g., 64k) of Hi-DOS memory, but only
        if the user doesn&#x27;t need expanded memory.  

        Examples: CONTAQ 82C591 (no hardware EMS support)
                  Headland/G2 (many do have hardware EMS however)
                  ACC Microelectronics (many do have hardware EMS)
                  USA Integration (USAi) (no hardware EMS)


        3.3 Overly Complex Control       

        The  Last Byte Memory Manager software is table-driven, making it
        relatively   easy   to   adapt  to  different  memory  controller
        architectures, but there are limits!   

        Examples: Zymos/Appian System 90 chipset
                  United Microelectronics Corp UM82C384, &#x27;388, &#x27;389
                  Forex Computer Corp. FRX36C100



        Copyright (C) 1990-94, Key Software Products. All Rights Reserved


        Oct 09, 1994      SHADOW RAM MEMORY CONTROLLERS                17


                  Silicon Integrated System (SiS) 85C310.


        3.4 Locked Configuration Registers       

        Some  memory  controllers  are  designed  so  that  they  can  be
        &quot;locked&quot;  at the end of the main bios initialization, requiring a
        hardware  reset  to  unlock,  and  thus  preventing The Last Byte
        Memory Manager from accessing the controller.  

        Examples: Intel 82335, 82335SX


        3.5 Configuration I/O Ports Reassigned      

        Some  memory  controllers  are  designed so that the &quot;index/data&quot;
        pair  of I/O ports used to access the configuration registers can
        be  reassigned  to  different  I/O  addresses.   This  makes  the
        configuration  registers  effectively  inaccessible  to  The Last
        Byte  Memory  Manager since it has no way of knowing what new I/O
        port addresses may have been established within the main bios.  

        Examples: Texas Instruments TACT84500
                  GS Technology GS62CS03






























